  "subtitle": "This month's VMA goes to [LINK:1963:FF_Annual_1|FF Annual 1] with Sue Storm coming to tears over her original and \"expensive Dior and Saks Fifth Avenue dresses\" being ruined --\"Men!&nbsp; You're <i>all</i> beasts!\"\n\nHonorable Mention is awarded to the miniature reel-to-reel tape recorder hidden in Iron Man's suit from [LINK:1963:TOS_46_iron0|TOS #46], <i>heh</i>.",
  "review_text": "This month had a whopping nine graded stories, for a final average of just over [SPAN: severity=info; fontsize=large; fonttype=bold; text=x.xx], which was about one-and-a-quarter points more than last month.&nbsp; Five of them were, in fact, even above mid-grade, with the solid FF Annual and monthly issues both playing a role in boosting the overall quality.&nbsp; The good ASM and strong initial efforts by the two new books helped offset the four <i>Journey into Strange Tales of Suspense to Astonish</i> books, whose content remained comparatively poor\n\nI really do think there is something structurally wrong with the idea of balancing a superhero story with a couple of back-up tales (which are sometimes mildly humorous but only rarely interesting).&nbsp; I believe it would be better to abandon the back-up tales, which I guess they eventually did, turning three of them into half-and-half books, with <i>Journey Into Mystery</i> staying focused on Thor and Asgard.&nbsp; But that is still to come.\n\nTaken as a whole however, the month provided over reader-level quality and several genuinely interesting reads.\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** SUMMARY_BEGIN ***\n*** THIS MONTH ***0 graded stories over 0 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 0 grade character issue weight0.00*** LAST MONTH ***7 graded stories over 7 issues...TOTAL WEIGHT: 5 grade character issue       weight 8.5   asm       ASM #4      1.00 5.0   iron      TOS #45     0.75 4.5   ff        FF #18      1.00 4.5   torch     ST #112     0.50 3.5   torch     ST Annual 2 0.75 2.5   ant       TTA #47     0.50 2.0   thor      JIM #95     0.504.78\n*** SUMMARY_END ***]",
  "letters_page": "[HANG0] * New titles Avengers and X-Men join the ranks of Marvel, which also introduce both groups\n[HANG0] * Introductions of Magneto and Rama-Tut highlight the list, with Lady Dorma, Warlord Krang, Porcupine, Crimson Dynamo and Dorrie Evans also featured.\n[HANG0] * Sub-Mariner's origin and first invasion attempt of the surface world\n[HANG0] * Dr. Doom's appearance in ASM\n\n[DEVNOTE: *** INTRODUCTION_BEGIN ***\n*** INTRODUCTION_END ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_BEGIN ***]\n[DEVNOTE: *** HIGHLIGHTS_END ***]",
  "ownership": "Marvel catches its breath long enough to publish the standard six issues:\n[HANG0] * Things get hot for Thor\n[HANG0] * Things get even <i>hotter</i> for Iron Man\n[HANG0] * Ant-Man decides that being small just won't cut it\n[HANG0] * Spider-Man faces a new menace with a tail\n[HANG0] * The Fantastic Four have to deal with a molecular menace\n[HANG0] * And \"<i>Holy 1940s, Batman!\" </i>is that [SPAN: severity=info; fonttype=bold; text=Captain America] I see fighting the Human Torch?&nbsp; <b><i>What?</i></b><i></i>"
}